Saphira musl port: provide PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE_NP.

musl supplies only the POSIX PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE; the _NP spelling
is a glibc extension (identical value on Linux). Upstream maps it only
for Solaris; extend the fallback to any libc lacking the extension.
Saphira builds musl-only, so the glibc-enum interaction is moot here.

--- a/src/lib/u/lock.c
+++ b/src/lib/u/lock.c
@@ -52,6 +52,9 @@
 #if defined (__SVR4) && defined (__sun)
 #define PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE_NP PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE
 #endif
+#ifndef PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE_NP
+#define PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE_NP PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE
+#endif
 
 void u_init_lock(void *data)
 {
